@startuml
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #2C3E50
    LifeLineBorderColor #2C3E50
    ParticipantBorderColor #2C3E50
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #ECF0F1
}

title Client-Side Security Guard and Access Control (DoNotHackMyApp)

actor "User" as User
participant "Protected Component\n(ListGenerator / EditFormGenerator)" as ProtectedView
participant "navigateToUnauthorized\n(DoNotHackMyAppHelper)" as GuardHelper
participant "useNavigate\n(React Router)" as Router
participant "DoNotHackMyApp\n(Access Denied View)" as SecurityShield

== 1. Pre-Render Interception ==

User -> ProtectedView: Attempts to render view (with props: actualUser, requiredAuth)
activate ProtectedView

ProtectedView -> GuardHelper: navigateToUnauthorized(checkAuth, actualUser, requiredAuth, navigate)
activate GuardHelper

== 2. Authorization Policy Evaluation ==

GuardHelper -> GuardHelper: Evaluate authorization policies
note right of GuardHelper
  Permission evaluation hierarchy:
  custom function, explicit bypass, or
  standard verification (ADMIN bypass / exact role).
  See activity diagram:
  "18_Flow_DoNotHackMyApp_Authorization_Verification"
end note

== 3. Access Resolution ==

alt Access Denied (userHasAuth === false)
    GuardHelper -> Router: navigate("/do-not-hack-my-app")
    activate Router
    Router -> SecurityShield: Renders lock screen
    activate SecurityShield
    SecurityShield --> User: Displays "Unauthorized Access" notice
    deactivate SecurityShield
    deactivate Router

    GuardHelper --> ProtectedView: Aborts rendering (return null)
    deactivate GuardHelper
    note right ProtectedView
      Aborts component rendering lifecycle
      when authorization criteria are not met.
    end note
else Access Granted (userHasAuth === true)
    GuardHelper --> ProtectedView: Continues normal execution
    deactivate GuardHelper

    ProtectedView --> User: Renders protected table or form
end

deactivate ProtectedView

@enduml
